
# Spring Boot Todo App

A simple CRUD Todo List web application built with Spring Boot using the MVC architecture.

This project was created as a learning exercise to understand how Spring Boot MVC compares with ASP.NET MVC, including models, controllers, views, repositories, services, database access, and migrations.

![Todo App Screenshot](./docs/image.png)

---

## Features

* Create a new todo
* View all todos
* Edit an existing todo
* Delete a todo
* Mark a todo as completed
* Persistent local database
* Database migrations with Flyway
* Simple responsive styling with CSS

---

## Tech Stack

* Java 21
* Spring Boot 4.1.1
* Spring MVC
* Spring Data JPA
* Hibernate
* Thymeleaf
* H2 Database
* Flyway
* Maven
* HTML
* CSS
* VS Code

---

## Project Architecture

The application follows a layered MVC architecture:

```text
Browser
   |
   v
Controller
   |
   v
Service
   |
   v
Repository
   |
   v
JPA / Hibernate
   |
   v
H2 Database
```

The project structure is:

```text
todoapp/
|
├── docs/
│   └── image.png
|
├── src/
│   ├── main/
│   │   ├── java/
│   │   │   └── com/
│   │   │       └── example/
│   │   │           └── todoapp/
│   │   │               ├── controller/
│   │   │               │   └── TodoController.java
│   │   │               │
│   │   │               ├── model/
│   │   │               │   └── Todo.java
│   │   │               │
│   │   │               ├── repository/
│   │   │               │   └── TodoRepository.java
│   │   │               │
│   │   │               ├── service/
│   │   │               │   └── TodoService.java
│   │   │               │
│   │   │               └── TodoappApplication.java
│   │   │
│   │   └── resources/
│   │       ├── db/
│   │       │   └── migration/
│   │       │       └── V1__create_todo_table.sql
│   │       │
│   │       ├── static/
│   │       │   └── css/
│   │       │       └── style.css
│   │       │
